    body: 'Good table manners are important in every culture. In China, we use chopsticks instead of knives and forks. When we eat, we should not point chopsticks at others because it is considered rude. We should also not stand chopsticks upright in a bowl of rice, as it resembles incense for the dead. It is polite to let elders eat first and to use both hands when passing dishes to others. In Western culture, people keep their hands on the table, not in their lap, and say "please" and "thank you." Understanding different table manners shows respect for other cultures and helps us behave properly in social situations.',
